plan:
Layer 1 (Cin=3): XLA builds patches with K=81 (pad 96) on sublanes and two output rows x 128 cols on lanes, (B,To,Ho/2,96,256);
  Pallas grid (B, To, Ho/32) does (32,96) @ (96,256) per row pair, f32 accumulate, bias+ReLU, bf16 out in (B,T,H,C,W) order.
Layer 2: patches (M=262144, 864) built by stacking 27 strided slices on a leading axis and one transpose (no minor-dim concat of 32-wide pieces);
  layers 3-6: channels-last im2col (64..512-wide pieces); all via a tiled (tm, tk) @ (tk, N) Pallas matmul with an f32 VMEM accumulator and fused bias+ReLU.
Head: one Pallas call does the spatial mean (averaging matmul), ReLU and the (512,128) Linear. Outside: only pads, slices, concats, transposes, reshapes.
Speed idea: remove A2's slow minor-dim-3/32 concatenations and its packed-row relayout; L1 keeps lanes dense instead of padding Cin=3 to 128.
